From c865851020e7cdb87ba7eb48359e98c45d7335c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Catrysse <jan.catrysse@geoxyz.eu>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 16:33:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve the wiki page hierarchy and include page attachments
 in the ZIP export.

The ZIP export added in #43978 flattens the wiki: every page becomes a
top-level <title>.txt, so the parent/child structure Redmine has is lost,
and pages whose titles sanitise to the same name need an (n) suffix that
the hierarchy would have made unnecessary.

The archive now mirrors the wiki instead: one directory per page, nested
by parent, holding that page's source.

An option on the ZIP export dialog adds each page's attachments to its own
directory, next to the source, so that a bare-filename reference such as
!diagram.png! resolves once the archive is unpacked. Attachments are opt-in
because their total size is checked against bulk_download_max_size, as
AttachmentsController#download_all does; the source-only export therefore
keeps working for a wiki whose attachments exceed the limit.

test_export_to_zip and test_export_to_zip_should_sanitize_non_portable_entry_name_characters
are updated for the new entry paths.
